&lt;h2&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of SumUp&#39;s Engineering, Product &amp;amp; Design organisation in &lt;strong&gt;São Paulo&lt;/strong&gt;, this role sits within the &lt;strong&gt;Product Growth team&lt;/strong&gt;, in close collaboration with the &lt;strong&gt;Sell Online tribe&lt;/strong&gt;, a globally distributed team working across regions. You&#39;ll help shape both merchant and cardholder facing experiences across our core Sell Online products — &lt;strong&gt;Payment Links, Online Store, Invoices, Bookings, Gift Cards and Order and Pay&lt;/strong&gt; — driving SMB merchant growth and experience across these product interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product strategy and day-to-day execution, collaborating closely with the squads within the &lt;strong&gt;Sell Online tribe&lt;/strong&gt;, with the &lt;strong&gt;Acquiring team in Brazil&lt;/strong&gt;, and other payment processing teams. Together, we&#39;ll make it easier for millions of small businesses to sell online with SumUp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent merchant and cardholder facing product initiatives across the Sell Online portfolio, with a focus on experience, conversion optimisation, activation, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Sell Online product strategy and roadmap, ensuring alignment with OKRs and growth KPIs, while acting as the voice of the Brazilian market — leading local discovery, benchmarking, and translating global products to local needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the Sell Online tribe, Acquiring, Payout, and payment processing teams to align on priorities and translate needs into clear product requirements — partnering with CRM, Online Marketing, and Sales on go-to-market execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product growth and adoption through experimentation, A/B testing, and continuous improvement, using data and analytics to track key metrics, identify areas of opportunity, and iterate on existing features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Design and UX Research to incorporate merchant insights into the product development cycle, ensuring experiences remain intuitive and effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business and operations teams to deliver high-impact solutions and ensure they are fully enabled to support the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll Be Great for This Role If&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;2–3 years of experience in Product Management&lt;/strong&gt; (or a closely related role), with a track record of collaborating with cross-functional teams to ship product improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are &lt;strong&gt;customer-centric and data-driven&lt;/strong&gt;, comfortable using metrics to inform prioritisation and measure impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;working knowledge of SQL or another data querying language&lt;/strong&gt; and can use data to back up your decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a strong communicator who can break down complex topics into clear, structured narratives for diverse audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a &lt;strong&gt;hands-on and pragmatic mindset&lt;/strong&gt;: proactive, curious, and always seeking better ways to deliver value to merchants — you&#39;re comfortable rolling up your sleeves and getting things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in collaborative, globally distributed and multicultural environments, working effectively across regions and time zones, and are comfortable navigating a fast-paced environment with evolving priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent in &lt;strong&gt;English&lt;/strong&gt;, written and verbal.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ecommerce products, payment flows, or online checkout environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with growth frameworks, experimentation, A/B testing, or CRM-driven product strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working in fintech or similarly fast-moving, regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with API-based or technically complex product environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You Should Join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our dynamic &lt;strong&gt;São Paulo&lt;/strong&gt; hub in the heart of the city. This involves an office-first setup.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 &lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion:&lt;/strong&gt; be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced.&lt;/p&gt;
