&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CoreOps Senior Manager – Payments, Non-Payments &amp;amp; Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in the everyday hero. Those who have the courage to follow their passion and who have the strength and determination to realize their dreams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Small business owners are at the heart of all we do, so we&#39;re creating powerful, easy-to-use financial solutions to help them run their businesses. With a founder’s mentality and a &#39;team-first’ attitude, our diverse teams across Europe, South America and the United States work together to ensure that small business owners can be successful doing what they love.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role leads Core Operations (CoreOps) in LATAM, owning the operational performance and resilience of three core areas: Payments, Non-Payments, and Enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CoreOps Leader is accountable for ensuring that critical operational processes function reliably, efficiently, and at scale. This includes the end-to-end transaction lifecycle, non-transactional products that complement the core payments offering, and the onboarding and risk processes that enable sustainable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role, not an execution role. The primary responsibility is to set direction, establish clear ownership, and enable teams to perform, ensuring operational stability while supporting the company’s long-term growth and profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a cross-functional CoreOps team, structured around Payments, Non-Payments and Enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the stability and resilience of own acquiring operations, including settlement, payouts, and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for payout execution, ensuring funds are delivered on time, predictably, and with minimal manual intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee operational performance of non-transactional products such as the SumUp Business Account, subscriptions, and electronic invoicing (DTE), ensuring they meet defined quality and reliability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure onboarding, activation, and risk processes operate efficiently while complying with evolving regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear accountability, KPIs, and ownership across the team, enabling autonomy and reducing single points of failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Finance and Accounting to ensure operational costs, settlements, and reconciliation are accurately reflected in financial reporting and P&amp;amp;L.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Support, Customer Success, Acquisition, Compliance, Product, and Engineering teams to align operational execution with business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement and contribute to regional initiatives, including cross-market operational synergies and shared operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Must Have&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading teams in complex operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills, with the ability to delegate ownership, build trust, and drive execution through others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, with experience working across Operations, Finance, Accounting, Compliance, Engineering or Commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in ambiguous, high-impact environments and prioritize across multiple critical workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of the payments industry at a conceptual and operational level (e.g. acquiring, payment flows, settlement), sufficient to make informed decisions without starting from zero.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, payments, or financial services operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to non-payments products such as digital accounts, subscriptions, invoicing, or lending.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regional or multi-market setups, particularly in LATAM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory or onboarding-related operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to lead one of the most critical operational areas in LATAM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-impact role with direct influence on merchant experience, financial performance, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomy to shape team structure, operating model, and execution standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, purpose-driven environment with global exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CoreOps Payments cell is the operational and data backbone of SumUp&#39;s acquiring business in Latin America — responsible for reconciliation, cost visibility, and the data infrastructure that keeps payment operations running accurately every day. This role sits at the heart of that work: owning the models, pipelines, and automation that the whole cell depends on to make sound decisions. It&#39;s a high-ownership position with real scope — you&#39;ll be building and stabilising critical data infrastructure in a space where the work directly shapes how SumUp manages and optimises its own acquiring processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own and maintain the data models and pipelines that support clearing-to-settlement reconciliation, processing cost visibility, and multi-acquiring analytics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and stabilise operational dashboards and alerts that feed day-to-day decisions across the Payments cell&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support accounting closures with reliable, automated data pipelines, reducing manual effort and increasing accuracy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reduce operational data work through automation, alerting, and standardised processes as the team scales to new markets and acquirers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Act as a technical bridge across CoreOps cells and with global teams, sharing best practices and translating operational needs into data solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience building and maintaining data models and pipelines using SQL, dbt, or equivalent tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong ability to work with raw, complex financial or transactional data and turn it into reliable, operational outputs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with reconciliation processes or financial data workflows, with a detail-oriented approach that prioritises accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfort working in ambiguous environments, able to build structure and define processes where little currently exists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Intermediate-to-advanced English proficiency, with the communication skills to work effectively across technical and non-technical stakeholders in a multi-market environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Santiago office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;br&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget that you can use to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖&amp;nbsp; 20 days of paid leave, plus public holidays and special leave days&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;🏥 Health and life coverage: in partnership with Zurich, we offer health insurance, including optical and dental and life insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻 Extra allowances: tax-free support for meals, childcare, transportation, and home internet&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h1 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Corporate Tax Manager&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://youtu.be/gqtjm5NUXs0?si=t7YARvQWQHHidD_z&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Take a look inside our Sofia office 🎬&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp&#39;s European Tax team is responsible for corporate income tax and transfer pricing compliance across 35+ entities — a function that sits at the heart of the company&#39;s financial integrity and growth. As SumUp moves into a tax-payable position and prepares for the next stage of its journey, the direct tax domain has never been more critical or more visible. This role is the primary owner of that domain: you&#39;ll design the compliance framework, ensure every filing is accurate and on time, and build the controls infrastructure that underpins sound tax governance. If you&#39;re looking for a role where your technical expertise has real, measurable impact, and where you can shape a function rather than just maintain one, this is it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own end-to-end Corporate Income Tax compliance across all European entities and Australia, including filing design, instalment calculations, deadline management, and audit-ready documentation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the remediation of outstanding direct tax compliance items, building a structured backlog register with risk ratings and a clear remediation plan&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish and maintain a 4-eyes quality control framework across all CIT, withholding tax, Pillar 2, and Country-by-Country Reporting filings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain a master compliance calendar with jurisdiction-specific workflows, ensuring the compliance cycle runs predictably and without last-minute escalations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advise on complex direct tax matters — including transfer pricing, M&amp;amp;A activity, and restructuring — and act as the primary point of contact for Finance, Accounting, and Controlling teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong, hands-on experience in corporate income tax compliance across multiple jurisdictions in a multinational environment, gained both in-house and in an advisory capacity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep knowledge of CIT mechanics, withholding tax obligations, and a solid working understanding of Pillar 2 / GloBE rules and Country-by-Country Reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to read, challenge, and discuss financial statements independently, with a strong accounting foundation and familiarity with the interaction between management accounts and statutory accounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced Excel skills (PivotTables, VLOOKUP, Power Query) and strong ERP experience, preferably SAP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfort working in a fast-moving, evolving environment where priorities shift and the ability to manage multiple jurisdictions simultaneously is essential&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Sofia office. This involves an office-first setup 🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced 🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Options Programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success 📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education 🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 20 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days 🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service 🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 37 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;our diverse team&lt;/a&gt; of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our core values&lt;/a&gt; lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;careers website&lt;/a&gt;, and follow our journey on &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;TikTok&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is On Site&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Support Agent - Dutch speaker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At SumUp, we are driven to empower small businesses across the globe by de-hassling their lives and helping them to succeed. Our vision as a global FinTech company is to build the first-ever global card acceptance brand, and we are well on our way as small businesses in over 33 countries around the world rely on SumUp to get paid. To get there, we are putting together an awesome team that is committed to one another and to our merchants. You could be our missing link! Help us bring card acceptance to the masses!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will support our POS users!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guarantee the management and prioritisation of the customer demands and solve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offer an unwavering quality to our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage diverse requests&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure an adequate communication and accompany the internal teams in case of major incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be in contact with the customers in different channels (calls, emails, chats)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be great for this position if you’re:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in Dutch and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communicator and customer-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keen to evolve in a start-up environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working on a Shift rotating schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Happy to work at our Amsterdam HQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Amsterdam office. This involves an office-first setup.&lt;/p&gt;
