&lt;p&gt;SumUp is on a mission to empower small businesses worldwide with simple and affordable tools. Today, more than 4 million businesses across 37 markets rely on SumUp to manage payments, finances, and customer relationships.&amp;nbsp;With a team of over 4,000 people from more than 90 nationalities, SumUp is built on global collaboration, inclusivity, and a continuous learning culture. They&#39;re committed to creating an environment where everyone belongs, feels supported, and can grow — no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CoreOPS team is the operational backbone behind SumUp&#39;s product ecosystem in Latin America, made up of three focused cells: Payments, Non-Payments, and Enablement. This role sits at the heart of the Non-Payments cell, where products like the SumUp Business Account, collections/subscriptions, and electronic invoicing (DTE) are growing fast and need a dedicated owner to make sure they run reliably and improve continuously. If you&#39;re energised by complex operational challenges and want to see the direct impact of your work on merchants and product teams, this is a role with real scope and meaningful ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain operational KPIs and dashboards across Non-Payments products (Business Account, subscriptions/collections, and electronic invoicing/DTE), ensuring clear visibility of product health across Chile, Peru, Colombia, and Mexico&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define minimum operational standards (SLOs, SLAs, error thresholds) together with product owners, track performance against them, and coordinate corrective actions when deviations arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key operational routines such as reconciliations, exception handling, and periodic checks, while supporting the design of new processes that improve reliability and merchant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the operational point of contact for external providers, using data and clear metrics to raise incidents, negotiate fixes, and prioritise improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Enablement, Finance, and Support teams to deliver data-driven insights, align on improvement roadmaps, and identify opportunities for automation and better monitoring across Non-Payments products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and hands-on experience working with operational or product data to identify patterns, risks, and actionable opportunities — including SQL and BI tools such as Looker, Power BI, Tableau, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure complex problems, set clear priorities, and translate data into decisions that teams can act on with a hypothesis-driven approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting cross-functional stakeholders and communicating clearly and concisely, in both Spanish and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across multiple products and initiatives simultaneously, adapting quickly as priorities and products evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive ownership mindset — someone who doesn&#39;t just flag problems but drives them through to resolution, with a strong focus on operational quality and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, payments, or financial services operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to digital financial products such as digital accounts, subscriptions, invoicing, or lending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with subscription billing, recurring payments, or dunning processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of tax/e-invoicing concepts (DTE or equivalent) in LATAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌍 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Santiago office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget that you can use to advance your career through further education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏖 Generous time off: 20 days of paid leave, plus public holidays and special leave days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏥 Health and life coverage: in partnership with Zurich, we offer health insurance, including optical and dental and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💻 Extra allowances: tax-free support for meals, childcare, transportation, and home internet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/li&gt;
