&lt;p&gt;SumUp&#39;s Global Operations team is in the middle of a deliberate transformation - moving from reactive issue resolution to a proactive merchant happiness engine.&amp;nbsp;To get there, we&#39;re separating our Customer Support and Customer Success functions so each can be led with focus, clarity, and the right commercial logic. That means we&#39;re building this Director of Customer Support EMEA role from the ground up: full ownership of a 270+ person multilingual organisation, a clear mandate to raise the bar on quality and efficiency, and the opportunity to embed AI into how support actually works — not as a future ambition, but as a present-day competitive advantage. If you&#39;ve scaled large support organisations before and want to do it again and have a direct impact on the lives of millions of small businesses, this is the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full Customer Support strategy for EMEA: setting direction, performance targets, and the operating model for a 270+ person multilingual organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive measurable improvement across CSAT, First Contact Resolution, and Average Handle Time, building a consistent performance culture through clear goals, regular reviews, and coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the integration of AI and automation into day-to-day support operations, ensuring the team is equipped to work smarter and that human effort is focused where it has the most impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the merchant at senior leadership level, using data and customer insight to influence product decisions, reduce inbound contact volume, and improve self-serve resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Operations, Product, and Finance to align support priorities with company-wide goals and to make the case for the right investments at the right time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading and scaling large, internationally distributed customer support organisations, ideally in a high-growth tech (or fintech) environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving measurable improvements in CSAT, SLA performance, and operational efficiency, with a data-driven approach to performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial mindset, with the ability to balance short-term service targets against longer-term structural improvements to tooling, self-serve, and team capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional stakeholder management skills, with confidence communicating across seniority levels - from team leads to Executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI adoption, support platform optimisation, or large-scale operational transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Barcelona office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;/li&gt;
