&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Junior Payroll Partner&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our People Operations and Payroll team keeps SumUp running smoothly behind the scenes, making sure every SumUpper is paid accurately and on time, every month. Based in Berlin, you&#39;ll sit within the Northern Europe People Ops and Payroll team, working closely with a Senior Payroll Partner who brings deep expertise in German payroll, as well as colleagues across People Operations, and our external payroll provider.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role where precision really matters. You&#39;ll own the day-to-day operational payroll activities for Germany, building your expertise in German payroll legislation while playing a critical part in keeping our employees&#39; trust. As SumUp continues to grow, there&#39;s real scope to expand into additional payrolls across Europe over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9DG64C3moeQ&quot;&gt; Take a look at our Berlin office&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support all stages of the monthly German payroll cycle, from preparing and validating inputs through to reconciliation and submission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to employee payroll queries through our ticketing system, resolving them accurately and promptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with People Operations to maintain accurate employee payroll records and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support payroll compliance with German tax, labour, and social security legislation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify and improve payroll processes, reducing manual work where possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both German and English, written and spoken, is something you bring to the table&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting payroll processes or working with payroll-related data is part of your background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills, including Pivot Tables, XLOOKUP/VLOOKUP, and IF statements, are part of your toolkit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle confidential information with a high level of discretion and integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in a detail-oriented, deadline-driven environment while staying organised and accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine curiosity to develop expertise in German payroll legislation and a proactive approach to learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office. This involves an office-first set up&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💶 A corporate pension scheme where we match up to 20% of your contributions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days 🏙 Numerous other benefits such as Urban Sports Club subsidy, Kita placement assistance, subsidised office lunches&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service 🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 38 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI&quot;&gt; our diverse team&lt;/a&gt; of over 4,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/&quot;&gt; Our core values&lt;/a&gt; lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers website&lt;/a&gt;, and follow our journey on&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup&quot;&gt; TikTok&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About the team:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The People Ops &amp;amp; Payroll Eastern Europe team keeps the engine running for SumUppers across the region — making sure every hire, change, and payroll cycle is handled accurately, on time, and with care. In Bulgaria alone, we support 520+ employees, and as the business continues to grow, reliable People Ops execution is what makes that growth feel seamless for the people living it every day. This role sits at the heart of that — owning the day-to-day administration for SumUp Bulgaria, being a dependable point of contact for employees and managers, and helping us build a better, more consistent People Ops experience as we scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;The role is set to start as a one year fixed-term contract.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎥 Take a look at our &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://youtu.be/gqtjm5NUXs0?si=t7YARvQWQHHidD_z&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Sofia office&lt;/a&gt; to get a feel for where you&#39;d be working.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage employee lifecycle processes end-to-end — from hiring and onboarding documentation through to contract changes, absences, and offboarding&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keep employee data accurate and up to date in Workday, ensuring readiness for audits and compliance checks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support the monthly payroll cycle by collecting, validating, and submitting payroll inputs on time, coordinating with our external payroll provider&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Handle routine employee and manager queries with a service mindset, escalating more complex cases when needed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to process improvements, documentation, and data quality routines — including spotting opportunities for automation&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You will be great for this role if…&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a foundational understanding of Bulgarian employment law, social security and payroll requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate strong attention to detail and a genuine commitment to data accuracy, even when managing high volumes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You feel comfort working with HRIS and operational tools, and have an interest in automation and process improvement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You handle confidential employee information with professionalism and discretion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you have a service-oriented mindset, clear and professional communication, and sound judgment about when to escalate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a professional working proficiency in English.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 1 year of experience in People Operations or HR administration, or a similar role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And as a plus will be any exposure to payroll processes or tools such as Workday, Notion, or Jira.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
