&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Embedded Marketing team sits within the broader Engagement organisation at SumUp, working at the intersection of brand, CRM, and customer communications. We&#39;re responsible for the design infrastructure that powers how millions of small business owners experience SumUp across email, in-app messages, promotional banners, and campaign landing pages. This role exists because CRM design demand has grown significantly and we&#39;re ready to replace a fragmented freelance setup with something more strategic: a permanent, embedded design partner who can own the craft end-to-end. If you&#39;re motivated by building things from scratch, working at pace, and seeing your work reach a global audience of merchants, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the end-to-end design process for CRM communications across email, in-app, inbox, promotional banners, and campaign landing pages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain CRM templates in Figma, including components, channel-specific guidelines, and a visual asset library that non-designers can navigate independently&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate brand guidelines into every CRM channel, acting as the quality gate before assets go live on high-visibility campaigns such as newsletters and brand campaigns&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate closely with CRM Content Managers and Strategists to bring briefs to life, managing a consistent weekly delivery cycle across multiple concurrent requests&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monitor design trends and proactively propose improvements to CRM&#39;s design language and visual standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven portfolio demonstrating design work across marketing or communication channels such as email, banners, and landing pages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong proficiency in Figma, including the creation and maintenance of components, templates, and shared libraries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to apply brand guidelines consistently across multiple formats and channels, with a sharp eye for detail and quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience collaborating with non-designers, translating briefs into clear, effective visual outputs within tight timelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfort working in a high-volume environment, managing multiple concurrent requests while maintaining consistent delivery standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office. This involves an office-first setup 🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced 🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success 📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education 💶 A corporate pension scheme where we match up to 20% of your contributions 🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days 🏋️ Numerous other benefits such as Urban Sports Club subsidy, Kita placement assistance, subsidised office lunches 🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service 🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
