&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Marketing Manager (Direct to Consumer)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is building a consumer financial product with a distribution advantage that almost no other fintech can replicate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than four million merchants use SumUp, and more than a billion consumers come into contact with our products each year. We now have the opportunity to turn that reach into one of the world’s largest consumer financial ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our consumer product is already live across six European markets. The next challenge is to grow it from an emerging proposition into a product used by millions of consumers, and this role will lead that journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the heart of that growth.&amp;nbsp;This role sits at the heart of that growth. As our new &lt;strong&gt;Senior Marketing Manager,&lt;/strong&gt; you’ll own the owned and earned strategies that win customers directly, from the website and PR to partnerships, social, and brand across all six markets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;. It&#39;s a rare chance to build a direct acquisition engine from scratch inside a small, ambitious team, competing head-to-head with some of the best-funded neobanks in Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own direct-to-consumer strategy across website, PR and comms, partnerships, social, events, and brand and out-of-home, across six markets through and beyond the brand campaign window&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the website into a high-converting acquisition surface, owning messaging, offers, content, localisation, and advertising across all markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive PR, comms, and partnership strategies that build the consumer brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up the retail and merchant-sales-channel motion for the consumer product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold and improve the direct cost-per-customer target, and report on direct-acquisition performance to feed channel-mix decisions&lt;/li&gt;
