&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;Senior Platform Engineer – US Platform Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍 Boulder, CO, USA | Full-time | Office First&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/ZF8A9onHQCE?si=c-GZnVUkrOATN2Jg&quot;&gt;Check out our Boulder office&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Team description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US Platform team is the engineering backbone that keeps SumUp&#39;s product teams moving. We build and maintain the cloud infrastructure, tooling, and developer environments that hundreds of engineers across the US depend on every day. As we grow, we&#39;re making a deliberate investment in senior expertise to raise the bar on how we build, standardize, and connect our platform work globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a pivotal role at the intersection of infrastructure and developer experience. You&#39;ll be the primary technical bridge between our US Platform team and our global Platform Infrastructure organization, ensuring both move in the same direction with shared standards, a unified codebase, and a clear roadmap. If you&#39;re energized by making complex systems simpler for the people who build on them, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement infrastructure-as-code solutions, driving automation of manual processes and improving deployment speed and reliability across the US engineering organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the technical connector between the US Platform team and the global Platform Infrastructure team, establishing shared standards, runbooks, and a joint technical roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve our monitoring, observability, and incident response processes, including cross-timezone on-call coordination and post-mortem practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal tooling and self-service capabilities that help product engineering teams deploy, monitor, and scale services independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the migration of US infrastructure into a unified, cohesive platform, treating our internal platform surfaces with the same intentionality we bring to customer-facing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in platform, DevOps, or infrastructure engineering at a senior level in complex, distributed environments (~8+ years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in AWS services (EC2, S3, RDS, VPC, IAM, EKS) and advanced Kubernetes, including cluster design, multi-tenant management, and upgrade strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Infrastructure as Code (Terraform and/or CloudFormation at scale) and CI/CD design using tools such as Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or ArgoCD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with service mesh technologies (Istio preferred), observability platforms (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK/OpenSearch), and proficiency in Go, Python, or JavaScript/TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across globally distributed teams, with the communication skills to influence both technical and non-technical stakeholders and the mindset to thrive in async, cross-timezone environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base Salary range for this position is $160-$185K annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Option Plan participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation will be finalized based on the candidate’s experience and location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Boulder office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/p&gt;
