&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People operations &amp;amp; payroll - Working Student (Berlin)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Berlin, Germany | Working student | Fixed-term&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Northern Europe People Enablement team and gain hands-on experience in a regional HR function at SumUp. As a Working Student, you&#39;ll support People Operations in Germany, helping manage contracts, HR administration, benefits, HR systems and payroll processes. It&#39;s an opportunity to build practical HR experience while contributing to a team that&#39;s shaping how People Operations are delivered across five countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎥 Get a feel for our Berlin office:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9DG64C3moeQ&quot;&gt; Berlin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle employee queries via our People team service desk and keep HRIS data accurate in Workday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage employment contract administration, including contract creation, amendments, and signature tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage benefits administration end to end — sign-ups, Workday updates, payroll communication, and invoices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organise, digitise, and file incoming physical post and sensitive employee documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the payroll team with data accuracy tasks and basic Excel-based reporting where capacity allows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both German and English (written and verbal) — essential for day-to-day communication and document handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a high level of accuracy when managing confidential information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with Excel, including pivot tables and VLOOKUP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple recurring tasks independently, with strong time management and organisational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in university for at least three semesters, with a proactive mindset and a genuine interest in People Operations or HR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside experienced People professionals, gain exposure to regional HR operations across multiple countries, and build valuable experience in the fast-growing fintech industry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office at Ostbahnhof&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Be part of an inclusive and collaborative environment where different perspectives are valued&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖️ 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days, pro-rated&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚵🏾‍♂️ Access health and well-being support through our Employee Assistance Programme, an Urban Sports Club subsidy, and fitness activities, including on-site gym access, yoga sessions, and team sports&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚆 Benefit from subsidised public transport with the Deutschlandticket, offering unlimited travel on local and regional transport across Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🥗 Enjoy partially subsidised office lunches and weekly breakfast&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Receive additional rewards through our employee referral programme when referring talents to join our team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
